[This is #7 in my reverse-alphabetical ascension geas, with Ran Rog Sam 
Tou Val Wiz having preceded this Pri. I might not have YAAP'ed the Ran,
though I did question the usefulness of the Longbow at the time.]

Lauri tromps in through the door of the demigods bar, pulls up a stool, and 
says to the barman, "here, put this on toast,

 S - a blessed tin of woodchuck meat

and make me a Red Eye [1] with this, please,

 W - a Scorpius egg

I have a headache." When the drink arrives, she stirs with

 V - a wand of wishing (1:1)


[ You know, never before in a game of nethack have I cried out "for the love 
of Manannan Mac Thingy, _another_ bloody wand of wishing!?". 'til now. ]

Lauri followed in the footsteps of Laura and Laure - except
they had descended into the Dungeons of Doom and not returned.
Soldier ants and giant mimics had sealed _their_ fates.

Lauri had in mind to keep her XP level low, and to let her
pet cat Morris do the fighting. Of course, you also want to
be level 2 or 3 so you have enough HP and spell power.

Lauri was lucky finding wands. Level 1 gave her a wand of speed
monster (promptly used on herself) and level 2 a wand of slow
monster (useful for packs of rothes?). No store on level 2 or
level 3, but there _was_ an iron wand of wishing! 0:3, no less.
3 ?oCharging, +3 GDSM, and 3 !oGA later, Lauri is looking pretty
buff. Good AC, at any rate:

Lauri the Aspirant           St:15 Dx:14 Co:14 In:14 Wi:20 Ch:13  Chaotic
Dlvl:3  $:229 HP:15(15) Pw:34(34) AC:-5 Exp:2 T:709

Lauri spent some time pondering what to do next, and then wished for +3 
[GoDex, +Id, +0 [HoB. This seemed like a pretty much guaranteed ascension, 
now, with at least 4 wishes from the castle wand. Had Lauri been a little 
less dim-witted, she would have saved the wish for the [HoB, since that's 
just trash once the quest artifact arrives.

DL4 yielded a Hawaiian shirt and elven boots, so she was now quiet, fast, and 
stunning in a lurid floral way. Fortunately the terry bathrobe and fuzzy 
slippers covered up most of it, for the shopkeepers. Now, trudging down to 
the Oracle and Sokoban brought her up to XL5 without yielding any temples, so 
it looked like protection just wasn't going to be her mainstay. The Oracle 
yielded no spellbooks, but a =SeeInvis, which turned out to be handy when the 
first orc with a wand of make invisible showed up.

Round about now, with most of an AK already, Lauri started thinking about 
conducts. Wishless is out, eh. Genoless is in. Polyless .. she'd already 
found a =PolyControl, as well (man, +Id is really really useful sometimes), 
so that's probably not a good idea. Silly stuff? What do priests _do_, 
anyway? Tins of priest meat of all opposing alignments crossed her mind, but 
that was a little gruesome even for her mind. Keeping her pet alive seemed 
like a plan. Extinctionist? Possibly, but only if I don't get bored.

Of course Morris the cat gets himself killed in the treasure room in Sokoban, 
so that plan is out as well. Let's go for a vanilla ascension.

When a chameleon appeared in Sokoban (they had a nasty tendency to appear 
only as liches or worse, it seems), a plan formed: get a (mini) herd of 
silver dragons. They're ridable, if she can find a saddle or some such. She 
laid three eggs, but life is really really tough for small dragons:

The baby silver dragon eats a silver dragon egg (laid by you).

We'll call him Puff, ok? Sokoban's prize was a shiny amulet, so Lauri is 
really glittery today. And in danger, too, of biting a cockatrice or some 
other nasty.

Lauri flew most of the way back up to the Gnomish mines, and turned back into 
an elf. Puff was having a great time chawing down gnomes and things in the 
mines, and minetown itself was a bones pile from a previous priest (Laura) 
who had had a run-in with an owlbear. That was no problem now, and Puff ate 
most of the shopkeepers, so Lauri could buy 5 levels of protection from the 
priest. Then Puff ate the poor bugger, and Lauri went on a sacfest. Having 
+CreateMonster in your starting inventory makes things easy that way.

First prayer to Poseidon got Lauri crowned. Oops. Oh well, some of those 
intrinsics she hadn't got yet, anyway. More sacrifices yielded Stormy.

Finally, DL12 yielded another temple. So back up to minetown to fetch the 
gold, then all the way back down again, only to discover that Puff had eaten 
the priest while Lauri wasn't looking. Moved all the stuff there anyway, 
since it's a good stash location, and wrested a last charge for a (BoH.

There were three more altars on the way down to Medusa, but nothing really 
useful. Medusa's level was the one with the Titan -- hostile, and it also 
promptly summoned a mind flayer that snacked on Lauri's brain [2]. Drat. Back 
up to remap, and to pick up that tin of grease somewhere.

After wandering around a little, Lauri reached XL13 and quaffed her one 
potion of gain level, so she would be ready to do the quest .. although? 
This Nalzok fellow sounds pretty tough. She spent some time looking in all 
the chests in the graveyard, though, and lo! Another wand of wishing. 0:2.

[ At this point, since this is only the third wand of wishing I've found 
lying around in the dungeon since I started my current reverse-alphabetical-
geas, I was thinking "what are the odds?" ]

Since /WoW are more plentiful (2 so far) that ?EA (0 so far), wish for some 
of them, and after a little play with a magic marker and more scrolls, Lauri's
shiny AC was down to -30. Nalzok respects scare monster, so that was trivial, 
swapping in the Mitre and doing some more enchanting got her AC down to -40. 

Taking the fast elevator down to below Medusa, Lauri walked back up, and gave 
the old hag the stern talking-to she's needed for years. The Titan was left 
for later, possibly fodder for Orcus' wand. The castle held two Liches and 
two Disenchanters, icky, and since Lauri had no way of getting _into_ the 
castle, she wished for =levitation and =free, then went round the backside 
and kicked ass. Puff bit it in this confrontation, so she wished for a wand 
of undead turning too (since there had been none so far). 

The castle wand was 0:2.

The valley was a bit of a walkthrough, saved the priest from Ravenous Puff, 
some wraiths contributed to XL20 -- Lauri decided she'd go as high level as 
she could manage then, and see what the fuss was about high-level monsters. 
Found a +4 ring of increase damage. Can you eat those things?

Things to do with the wishes from the castle wand: saddle + archons, to 
arrive in style. Lauri wished for a +MagicMapping to make Gehennom bearable,
then went back up to Medusa to deal with the Titan.

[ It was at this point, while exploring the little islands on Medusa, that I 
cried out "for the love of Manannan Mac Thingy, _another_ bloody wand of 
wishing!?". For there was a 0:1 lying around, too. ]

Lauri was lazy and had no blank scrolls handy, so she wished for more scrolls 
of charging, and a figuring of an Archon. Puff ate the Titan, and then all 
the gremlins who had been multiplying. Wished for 3 tins of tengu meat to 
finally get TC. The Archon has Sunsword, so he's a portable light source. 

Foolish Puff ate a doppelganger corpse and turned into a paper golem. It took 
a few charges from the wands of poly to turn him back into a baby blue 
dragon. What's a color change between friends? Must remember to get a saddle
for him when he grows up again.

.. and so Lauri had a rather unremarkable trudge down through Gehennom, made 
more so by the fact that Yeeno and Jubi had been summoned in minetown and led 
to mines end. Asmodeus was paid off, and then Lauri decided that giving money 
to leering men with icky goatees was a bad idea, and she smacked Baal'z ass 
hard. Vlad was an afterthought, the Wizard was too, since she saved one 
cockatrice corpse from the treasure zoo to give him. Boot to the head! Yeah 
yeah! Now what Canadian TV show was that from?

O yeah, now that Rodney is departed, we have a problem. Run downstairs, thump 
oomph bonk, Rodney back, double trouble, off them, another round of trouble, 
ouch. Good thing Lauri has a big shopping bag with all these potions of full 
healing she's found (do they allow bag ladies in the bar?). Had to wrest the 
amulet from his dead paws instead of doing the nice clean shoot priest cursed 
!GL thing she had in mind.

Up saw lots of Rodneys coming back, and not much mysterious force.

Did some final saccing and spellbook reading on DL12, swapped some stuff in 
her stash, and headed up.

Oh, by now Puff was no longer her running mate .. he hit a level teleporter 
and was never found. Same for two Archons, though they _were_ found (one 
still tame, other peaceful and retamed at the expense of 10 castings of charm 
monster). 

Now on the elemental planes, herding 3 Archons through the portal is a bit of 
a chore. No leashes either. Tamed lots of stuff on air which came along for 
the ride, and herded all of it through to fire, water, and astral. Water took 
quite some time, especially when Rodney came back and double-troubled twice. 
Astral had the right altar in the first branch, with Death, and Lauri just 
couldn't herd all the pets together so they'd ascend with her.

